# Architecture Cleanup Discipline (CO-ARCH-006) — PERMANENT

Catalyst One is evolving architecture — **not** carrying legacy for compatibility.

## Lifecycle (mandatory)

```text
Architecture → Implementation → Stabilization → BAT → Architecture Cleanup → Next Sprint
```

Every major architecture milestone ends with an **Architecture Cleanup Sprint** before the next feature sprint.

## Five-question removal test

For each obsolete-looking component:

1. Belong to current enterprise architecture?
2. Used by any active business workflow?
3. Another component already performs the same responsibility?
4. Can Catalyst One function correctly if removed?
5. Does removing it simplify the runtime?

If **No / No / Yes / Yes / Yes** → **delete permanently**.

## Forbidden

- Deprecate-and-leave
- Keep dormant “just in case”
- Compatibility adapters once no workflow needs them
- Dual Soft Go-Live + Registry write paths for the same Deal mutation

## Allowed during transition

Opportunity-before–Move to Deal may still use LoanFile-**shaped** projections until Category B cleanup redirects those workflows. Deal Workspace after Move to Deal must remain Enterprise Deal Registry only (`deal-pipeline-runtime`).

